{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2525","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2525","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2525\",\"parent_revision\":\"c9150ab6a109887048d129809e53d6e53189f2001c1935f79f19054957d37bed\",\"root_revision\":\"c9150ab6a109887048d129809e53d6e53189f2001c1935f79f19054957d37bed\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nresolve_section() in progressive_markdown/navigator.py silently returns the first match when multiple sections share a slug, but both its docstring and view_section()'s docstring advertise AmbiguousSectionRefError as a raise. The exception is exported from exceptions.py and documented as part of the public API surface, but the code path that would raise it does not exist. Callers cannot distinguish \\\"found exactly one section\\\" from \\\"found many, took first arbitrarily\\\". The fix is either: raise the exception when len(ids) > 1 (enforcing unambiguous slugs), or remove the exception from the docstrings and API surface and document the first-match behaviour explicitly.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **fix: ambiguoussectionreferror is documented as raised but never actually raised in resolve_section()** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Code review of progressive_markdown package \u2014 2026-05-31, surfaced by implementing agent during has_more computed_field fix\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-06-01\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"b9983fd177d3e91852cc80f023419fd17721e3486930f69e8a2896b49a8fa836\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCNpMw\"}"}